---
id: async-initial-values
title: Async Initial Values
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Forms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create the\nform until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback\nvalues. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience your UI\nneeds."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"wait-for-data-before-creating-the-editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for data before creating the editor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are complete."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// UserPage.tsx\nimport { Show } from 'solid-js'\nimport { createQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport { UserEditor } from './UserEditor'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nexport function UserPage(props: { userId: string }) {\n  const userQuery = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['user', props.userId],\n    queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${props.userId}`)\n      return response.json()\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Show\n      when={!userQuery.isError}\n      fallback={<p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>}\n    >\n      <Show when={userQuery.data} keyed fallback={<p>Loading…</p>}>\n        {(user) => <UserEditor user={user} />}\n      </Show>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// UserEditor.tsx\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nexport function UserEditor(props: { user: User }) {\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: props.user,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        form.handleSubmit()\n      }}\n    >\n      {/* fields */}\n    </form>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. The keyed\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Show"},{"type":"text","value":" recreates the editor when a different user object arrives."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the form before data arrives"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can instead call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createForm"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same component as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQuery"},{"type":"text","value":".\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are never\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Show } from 'solid-js'\nimport { createQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nexport function UserPage(props: { userId: string }) {\n  const userQuery = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['user', props.userId],\n    queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${props.userId}`)\n      return response.json()\n    },\n  }))\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: userQuery.data ?? emptyUser,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Show\n      when={!userQuery.isError}\n      fallback={<p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>}\n    >\n      <Show when={!userQuery.isPending} fallback={<p>Loading…</p>}>\n        <form\n          onSubmit={(event) => {\n            event.preventDefault()\n            form.handleSubmit()\n          }}\n        >\n          {/* fields */}\n        </form>\n      </Show>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because both integrations receive accessors, reading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userQuery.data"},{"type":"text","value":" inside\nthe form options accessor keeps the options reactive. When query data replaces\nthe fallback, TanStack Form applies the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the approach demonstrated by the repository's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/solid/query-integration"},{"type":"text","value":" example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Background refetches and record changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. In the fallback pattern, later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.reset(nextValues)"},{"type":"text","value":" deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely\nbecause a query refreshed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When switching to a different record, either recreate a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"wait-for-data-before-creating-the-editor","text":"Wait for data before creating the editor","level":2},{"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","text":"Create the form before data arrives","level":2},{"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","text":"Background refetches and record changes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy.\n\nThere are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create the\nform until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback\nvalues. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience your UI\nneeds.\n\n## Wait for data before creating the editor\n\nRender a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n`defaultValues` are complete.\n\n```tsx\n// UserPage.tsx\nimport { Show } from 'solid-js'\nimport { createQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport { UserEditor } from './UserEditor'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nexport function UserPage(props: { userId: string }) {\n  const userQuery = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['user', props.userId],\n    queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${props.userId}`)\n      return response.json()\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Show\n      when={!userQuery.isError}\n      fallback={<p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>}\n    >\n      <Show when={userQuery.data} keyed fallback={<p>Loading…</p>}>\n        {(user) => <UserEditor user={user} />}\n      </Show>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// UserEditor.tsx\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nexport function UserEditor(props: { user: User }) {\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: props.user,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        form.handleSubmit()\n      }}\n    >\n      {/* fields */}\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThis pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. The keyed\n`Show` recreates the editor when a different user object arrives.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nYou can instead call `createForm` in the same component as `createQuery`.\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback so `defaultValues` are never\n`undefined`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { Show } from 'solid-js'\nimport { createQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nexport function UserPage(props: { userId: string }) {\n  const userQuery = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['user', props.userId],\n    queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${props.userId}`)\n      return response.json()\n    },\n  }))\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: userQuery.data ?? emptyUser,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Show\n      when={!userQuery.isError}\n      fallback={<p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>}\n    >\n      <Show when={!userQuery.isPending} fallback={<p>Loading…</p>}>\n        <form\n          onSubmit={(event) => {\n            event.preventDefault()\n            form.handleSubmit()\n          }}\n        >\n          {/* fields */}\n        </form>\n      </Show>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nBecause both integrations receive accessors, reading `userQuery.data` inside\nthe form options accessor keeps the options reactive. When query data replaces\nthe fallback, TanStack Form applies the new `defaultValues` to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched.\n\nThis is the approach demonstrated by the repository's\n`examples/solid/query-integration` example.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` prop. In the fallback pattern, later `defaultValues` updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior.\n\nIf background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n`form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely\nbecause a query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching to a different record, either recreate a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: async-initial-values\ntitle: Async Initial Values\n---\n\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy.\n\nThere are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create the\nform until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback\nvalues. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience your UI\nneeds.\n\n## Wait for data before creating the editor\n\nRender a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n`defaultValues` are complete.\n\n```tsx\n// UserPage.tsx\nimport { Show } from 'solid-js'\nimport { createQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport { UserEditor } from './UserEditor'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nexport function UserPage(props: { userId: string }) {\n  const userQuery = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['user', props.userId],\n    queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${props.userId}`)\n      return response.json()\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Show\n      when={!userQuery.isError}\n      fallback={<p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>}\n    >\n      <Show when={userQuery.data} keyed fallback={<p>Loading…</p>}>\n        {(user) => <UserEditor user={user} />}\n      </Show>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// UserEditor.tsx\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nexport function UserEditor(props: { user: User }) {\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: props.user,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        form.handleSubmit()\n      }}\n    >\n      {/* fields */}\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThis pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. The keyed\n`Show` recreates the editor when a different user object arrives.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nYou can instead call `createForm` in the same component as `createQuery`.\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback so `defaultValues` are never\n`undefined`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { Show } from 'solid-js'\nimport { createQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\nimport type { User } from './types'\n\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nexport function UserPage(props: { userId: string }) {\n  const userQuery = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['user', props.userId],\n    queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n      const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${props.userId}`)\n      return response.json()\n    },\n  }))\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: userQuery.data ?? emptyUser,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Show\n      when={!userQuery.isError}\n      fallback={<p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>}\n    >\n      <Show when={!userQuery.isPending} fallback={<p>Loading…</p>}>\n        <form\n          onSubmit={(event) => {\n            event.preventDefault()\n            form.handleSubmit()\n          }}\n        >\n          {/* fields */}\n        </form>\n      </Show>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nBecause both integrations receive accessors, reading `userQuery.data` inside\nthe form options accessor keeps the options reactive. When query data replaces\nthe fallback, TanStack Form applies the new `defaultValues` to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched.\n\nThis is the approach demonstrated by the repository's\n`examples/solid/query-integration` example.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` prop. In the fallback pattern, later `defaultValues` updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior.\n\nIf background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n`form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely\nbecause a query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching to a different record, either recreate a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive.\n"}
